s=dict(action='continue',candidate_id='C_accept_history',rationale='Register the first sourced acceptance-history question together with a usable two-core map. No obligation or execution result is asserted.',sources=sources,map_path='map.json',question=q,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['S_accept','S_prepare','S_recover_select','S_start_recovery','S_receive'],answered='The captured implementation connects acceptance to recovery through Instance phase, value ballot and ordering attributes. Accept updates the attributes and both ballots without setting ACCEPTED; Prepare exports the retained phase, and recovery branches on it. Existing ballot and committed-state guards constrain the suspicion. TCP decoding launches per-message delay goroutines before type-channel delivery, so a future schedule must distinguish receipt from handler dispatch. This is source-only learning, with no executed witness or settled obligation.',remaining=q['unknowns'],understanding='updated',rationale='The missing producer-side phase update matters because a read consumer explicitly distinguishes accepted from preaccepted history. A legal prefix and narrowly grounded predicate are the next discriminator.'))
